//! The `grid-column-end` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property specifies
//! a grid item's end position within the grid column by contributing a line, a span, or nothing
//! (automatic) to its grid placement, thereby specifying the block-end edge of its `grid area`.
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: Contributes nothing to the grid item's placement, indicating auto-placement, an automatic
//! span, or a default span of `1`. This is the default value.
//!
//! Grammar: <grid-line>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-grid-2/#propdef-grid-column-end
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/grid-column-end
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Additional value descriptions: Microsoft (MIT).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

